     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §77-k, Gen Muni L",
    "lawSection": "General Municipal Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S5525\n\nSPONSOR: HARCKHAM\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the general municipal law, in relation to permitting the\nvillage of Croton-on-Hudson, Westchester county, to lease certain sports\nfield fences for advertisements\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of this legislation is to permit the Village of Croton-on-\nHudson to lease certain sports field fences for advertisements to raise\nrevenue.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSECTION 1. A new section 77-k is added to the General Municipal Law,\nwhich will allow the Village of Croton-on-Hudson to place advertising at\nDobb's Park, Duck Pond Park, Firefighters Memorial Field and David J\nManes Memorial Field.\n\nSECTION 2. Establishes the effective date.\n\n \nDIFFERENCE BETWEEN ORIGINAL AND AMENDED VERSION (IF APPLICABLE):\n\nNot applicable.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe village of Croton-on-Hudson wants the ability to lease space on the\nfences at several sports fields under their jurisdiction for the purpose\nof advertising. This will increase revenue for the Village of Croton-on-\nHudson Recreation and Parks Department, which will be utilized to\nimprove and better maintain said fields. This may also reduce the tax\nburden on village residents.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThis is new legislation.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nIncreased revenue for the village of Croton-of-Hudson.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
